  "title": "Panch Phoron Spiced Vegetables",
  "subtitle": "Bengali-spiced root vegetables with a five-seed tempering",
  "excerpt": "A mix of potato, sweet potato, carrot, and green beans are cooked with a tempering of cumin, mustard, and fennel seeds in the Bengali style. The spices go into hot oil first so they bloom before the vegetables are added. Serves four as a hearty side dish.",
